---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { COMPANY, SUB_PROCESSORS } from "../constants/legal";
---

<Legal title="Privacy" description="Which companies receive your data when you use EliseLAB, and what each one receives.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Last updated 22 November 2026.</p>
  <p>This page says what personal information EliseLAB collects, why, who else receives it, how long we keep it and how to have it deleted. EliseLAB is run by Lynkfire Limited, a company in New Zealand. We follow the New Zealand Privacy Act 2020.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your account.</strong> Your name, email address and a hashed password. We also keep your role in an account and the other members you invite.</li>
    <li><strong>Sign-in records.</strong> The IP address and browser details of your sessions, and the name, system and IP address of a computer you approve as a Runner.</li>
    <li><strong>Your work in EliseLAB.</strong> Repositories you add (their addresses and branch names), Scans, the reports and Findings a Runner sends back, the decisions and comments your team writes, and a list of what each Scan did, by label only. If you upload a zip file, we also hold the zip.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing.</strong> Your plan and subscription status. Your card details go to Stripe and we never see or store them.</li>
    <li><strong>Email we send.</strong> Invitations and security notices, such as a password reset or a Runner added to your account, sent from <span class="nowrap">no-reply@hello.eliselab.com</span>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not collect your source code from a Git repository. The Runner reads it on your computer. Only a zip file you upload to EliseLAB is stored by us.</p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <p>We use this information to run your account, run and show your Scans, take payment, keep EliseLAB secure, send the notices above and answer you when you write to us. We do not sell it and we do not use it for advertising. We do not use cookies for tracking, only to keep you signed in.</p>

  <h2>Sub-processors</h2>
  <p>EliseLAB sends some of your data to the companies below. Each one receives only what its row says.</p>

  <ul class="processors">
    {
      SUB_PROCESSORS.map((processor) => (
        <li>
          <h3>{processor.name}</h3>
          <p>{processor.purpose}</p>
          <p><strong>Receives.</strong> {processor.receives}</p>
          <p><strong>Never receives.</strong> {processor.neverReceives}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Your own AI provider</h2>
  <p>A Scan runs on your computer, in the Runner, with your own AI account. That provider is yours, not ours: you have your own agreement with it, and EliseLAB does not send your code to a model provider. What the provider does with the code the Runner shows it is covered by that agreement.</p>

  <h2>Signals</h2>
  <p>Signals are hints about a Finding or a decision, such as a possible duplicate. They are on for every account. An account admin can turn them off in Account settings, and turning them off stops new requests to TypeSafe. A Signal never changes a Finding, a decision or a pass or fail.</p>

  <h2>Sending information outside New Zealand</h2>
  <p>The companies above may process your information outside New Zealand. We use them only for the purposes in their rows.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A zip file you upload that no Scan has read is deleted 30 days after upload. A zip a Scan has read stays until you remove it. Removing a zip or a repository deletes its files and records.</li>
    <li>Reports, Findings, comments and Scan records stay for as long as your account exists. They have no expiry.</li>
    <li>Account details stay until the account is deleted.</li>
    <li>Stripe keeps its own payment records under its own rules.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your data and your rights</h2>
  <p>EliseLAB has no delete button for an account yet. To delete yours, email us at the address below. A person at Lynkfire Limited deletes the account by hand, within 20 working days of your request. That removes its members, repositories, Scans, Findings, comments, stored reports and uploaded zips. Stripe keeps its own payment records under its own policy.</p>
  <p>You may also ask us for the personal information we hold about you and ask us to correct it. We answer within 20 working days. If you think we have handled your information badly, tell us first. You may also complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner in New Zealand.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>Data moves over encrypted connections. Passwords are stored hashed. Access to an account depends on a role, and changes to Finding decisions and to the budget are recorded. No online service is perfectly secure, and we tell affected people if a breach is likely to cause them serious harm.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
  <p>When we change this page we change the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <address>
    {COMPANY.name}<br />
    {COMPANY.address.map((line) => <Fragment>{line}<br /></Fragment>)}
  </address>
  <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> to ask for deletion or to ask about your data.</p>
</Legal>
